<header><p class="enc-kicker">Institution</p><h1 class="enc-title">Eidsivating</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Eidsivathing</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Eidsivating was the law assembly (thing) of the inland <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/uppland">Upplands</a> of eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/norway">Norway</a> in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/middle-ages">Middle Ages</a>, meeting at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/eidsvoll">Eidsvoll</a>. Its law, the Eidsivating law, governed Romerike, Hedmark and other inland districts until King <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/magnus-vi-of-norway">Magnus the Lawmender</a>'s national law code of 1274 replaced the regional laws. It was one of the four great law-thing districts of medieval Norway.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/eidsivating.jpg" alt="Eidsivating" width="320" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Copyright © Harry Wad · CC BY 2.5 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Eidsivatinget_Eidsvoll_Norway.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
